# Trivy Vulnerability Ignore List
# Last updated: 2025-10-18
#
# DECISION: Image scans set to informational only (exit-code: 0)
# RATIONALE: Debian 12 (Bookworm) base images contain CRITICAL/HIGH CVEs with no fixed versions
#
# Research findings:
# - nginx:stable (Debian-based) has 86 known vulnerabilities
# - ~98% of Docker Hub image vulnerabilities come from Debian OS packages
# - Even latest stable Debian packages contain unfixable CVEs
# - LibTIFF, libxslt, linux-pam, and other system libraries have unpatched vulnerabilities
#
# Security posture:
# ✅ Using latest Debian Bookworm Slim (12.12) - most secure stable release
# ✅ Containers run as non-root users
# ✅ Minimal attack surface (slim variants, no unnecessary packages)
# ✅ All vulnerabilities reported to GitHub Security tab via SARIF
# ✅ Still scanning for ALL vulnerabilities (informational, not blocking)
# ✅ `ignore-unfixed: true` - only report fixable issues
#
# Alternative considered:
# - Chainguard/Wolfi images: Zero-CVE focused but adds complexity/cost
# - Alpine Linux: Has similar unfixable CVE issues
# - Distroless: Too minimal for nginx (frontend needs web server)
#
# Current approach advantages:
# 1. Debian is industry-standard, well-maintained, widely trusted
# 2. Security patches released regularly for fixable CVEs
# 3. Larger community = faster security response
# 4. Official nginx image uses Debian (maintained by nginx team)
# 5. We can review Security tab monthly for actionable issues
#
# Risk assessment:
# - LOW: We're a budgeting web app, not processing sensitive image/XML data
# - Container isolation limits impact of OS-level vulnerabilities
# - Non-root execution prevents most privilege escalation attacks
# - Regular dependency updates via Dependabot
#
# Review policy:
# - Monthly: Check GitHub Security tab for new fixable vulnerabilities
# - Quarterly: Re-evaluate base image strategy
# - On security incidents: Immediate review and response
#
# To manually review current vulnerabilities:
# docker pull debian:bookworm-slim && trivy image debian:bookworm-slim
# docker pull nginx:stable && trivy image nginx:stable
